---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

---

<Layout
  title="Solar Battery Storage Systems in Koh Chang, Thailand"
  description="Professional solar battery storage installation in Koh Chang. Energy storage systems, lithium-ion phosphate batteries, and backup power for Thai homes and businesses."
>
  <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
  <nav class="breadcrumbs container" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/BreadcrumbList">
      <li itemprop="itemListElement" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/ListItem">
        <a itemprop="item" href={`/`}><span itemprop="name">Home</span></a>
        <meta itemprop="position" content="1" />
      </li>
      <li itemprop="itemListElement" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/ListItem">
        <a itemprop="item" href={`/services/`}><span itemprop="name">Services</span></a>
        <meta itemprop="position" content="2" />
      </li>
      <li itemprop="itemListElement" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/ListItem">
        <span itemprop="name">Battery Storage</span>
        <meta itemprop="position" content="3" />
      </li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="hero hero--service">
    <div class="hero__content container">
      <h1>Solar Battery Storage Systems</h1>
      <p class="hero__subtitle">
        Store your solar energy for nighttime use, power outages, and true energy independence
        in Koh Chang and across Thailand.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__cta">
        <a href={`/contact/`} class="btn btn--primary">Get a Battery Storage Quote</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Stats -->
  <section class="stats container">
    <div class="stats__grid">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-card__number">95%</span>
        <span class="stat-card__label">Round-Trip Efficiency</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-card__number">10+</span>
        <span class="stat-card__label">Year Battery Lifespan</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-card__number">24/7</span>
        <span class="stat-card__label">Backup Power Available</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="section container">
    <div class="section__content">
      <h2>Energy Storage for Thai Solar Systems</h2>
      <p>
        Solar photovoltaic modules generate power during daylight hours, but most households
        and businesses in Thailand consume the majority of electricity in the evening -- after
        the sun has set. Without an energy storage system, excess daytime generation from your
        PV panels is exported to the grid at unfavorable rates or simply wasted. A properly
        sized solar battery bank solves this mismatch by capturing surplus energy for use when
        you actually need it.
      </p>
      <p>
        At Koh Chang Solar Cell, we design and install battery storage systems using modern
        lithium-ion phosphate (LiFePO4) technology. These batteries offer superior thermal
        stability compared to standard lithium-ion chemistries, making them ideal for Thailand's
        tropical climate where ambient temperatures regularly exceed 35 degrees Celsius. Our
        typical residential installations range from 5 kilowatt-hours to 20 kilowatt-hours
        of usable capacity, sized precisely to match your evening consumption patterns and
        critical load requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        Whether you operate a beach resort that cannot afford refrigeration downtime, a
        family home with medical equipment, or a commercial facility processing payments,
        battery backup ensures continuous operation during the grid outages that occasionally
        affect Koh Chang and other island communities. The combination of solar arrays and
        energy storage transforms your property from a passive consumer into an active,
        resilient power station.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How It Works -->
  <section class="section section--alt container">
    <div class="section__content">
      <h2>How Battery Storage Works</h2>
      <p>
        A complete battery storage installation involves several integrated components working
        in concert with your existing or new photovoltaic system. Understanding the technical
        process helps you make informed decisions about capacity, configuration, and investment.
      </p>
      <p>
        During daylight, your solar arrays feed DC power to a hybrid inverter equipped with
        Maximum Power Point Tracking (MPPT) charge controllers. The inverter's primary job
        is converting DC to AC for immediate household use, but the MPPT circuitry also routes
        surplus energy to your battery bank at the optimal charging voltage. Modern lithium-ion
        phosphate batteries charge efficiently between 80% and 95% round-trip efficiency,
        meaning very little energy is lost in the storage cycle compared to older lead-acid
        technologies that typically achieve only 70% to 80%.
      </p>
      <p>
        The battery management system (BMS) monitors each cell's state of charge, temperature,
        and depth of discharge. We typically configure residential systems to limit depth of
        discharge to 90% of rated capacity, preserving the 10% buffer that extends battery
        lifespan beyond 6,000 cycles -- roughly 15 to 20 years of daily use in Thailand. When
        grid power fails, the inverter automatically disconnects from the utility and switches
        to island mode within 10 to 20 milliseconds, fast enough that computers and medical
        equipment continue operating uninterrupted.
      </p>
      <p>
        For systems with net metering agreements, the battery operates in a "time-shift"
        strategy: charging from excess solar during the day, then discharging in the evening
        when grid electricity rates are highest. In off-grid configurations common on remote
        Koh Chang properties, the battery serves as the primary energy reservoir, sized to
        provide 2 to 3 days of autonomy during monsoon season when heavy cloud cover reduces
        solar generation by 60% to 80%.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why Thailand -->
  <section class="section container">
    <div class="section__content">
      <h2>Why Battery Storage Matters in Thailand</h2>
      <p>
        Thailand's electricity tariff structure makes battery storage financially compelling
        for solar owners. The Provincial Electricity Authority (PEA) uses a progressive rate
        where consumption above 150 kilowatt-hours per month costs significantly more per unit
        than baseline usage. Without storage, your exported daytime solar earns credits at the
        low baseline rate, while your evening consumption gets charged at the expensive upper
        tiers. A battery captures that value by moving your own solar energy to the evening
        when you would otherwise buy expensive grid power.
      </p>
      <p>
        The tropical climate presents unique challenges that our battery designs address
        specifically. Standard lithium-ion batteries degrade rapidly above 45 degrees Celsius,
        but the lithium-ion phosphate chemistry we specify maintains stable performance up to
        60 degrees Celsius -- well above ambient temperatures even in Thailand's hottest
        months. Our outdoor battery enclosures include passive ventilation and optional active
        cooling for installations where direct sun exposure cannot be avoided.
      </p>
      <p>
        Monsoon season, typically May through October, brings extended periods of heavy cloud
        cover and rain that reduce solar array output by 50% to 70% on the worst days. For
        properties relying entirely on solar, adequate battery capacity bridges these gaps.
        We size off-grid systems with a minimum 48-hour autonomy buffer, meaning your stored
        energy covers two full days of typical consumption without any solar input. Grid-tied
        systems with battery backup can operate with smaller banks since the grid serves as
        the ultimate backup during prolonged bad weather.
      </p>
      <p>
        Power reliability varies across Thailand. While Bangkok and major cities enjoy stable
        grids, island communities including Koh Chang experience occasional outages from
        transformer maintenance, cable damage, or supply constraints during peak tourist season.
        A battery-backed solar system eliminates the inconvenience and potential revenue loss
        these outages cause for hospitality businesses.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What You Get -->
  <section class="section section--alt container">
    <div class="section__content">
      <h2>What You Get with Our Battery Storage Service</h2>
      <p>
        Every battery storage installation from Koh Chang Solar Cell includes comprehensive
        service from initial assessment through ongoing support. We handle the technical
        complexity so you receive a reliable system that performs as promised.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our process begins with a detailed energy consumption analysis. We review your past
        12 months of electricity bills, identify your peak evening loads, and calculate the
        optimal battery capacity -- not oversized (wasting money on unused capacity) or
        undersized (leaving you dependent on grid power). For residential customers, this
        typically results in a 10 kilowatt-hour system costing 180,000 to 350,000 Thai Baht
        depending on brand and features. Commercial installations range from 50 kilowatt-hours
        upward, with pricing scaled accordingly.
      </p>
      <p>
        We supply only Tier 1 battery products from manufacturers with established track records
        in tropical climates. Current options include BYD, Pylontech, and Victron lithium-ion
        phosphate systems, all carrying 10-year warranties and 6,000+ cycle guarantees. The
        installation itself includes DC cabling with appropriate gauge sizing, fuse protection,
        battery enclosure (indoor or outdoor rated IP65), and integration with your existing
        or new inverter. We never reuse old cabling or mix incompatible battery generations in
        the same bank.
      </p>
      <p>
        The deliverable package includes a complete commissioning report showing actual
        round-trip efficiency measured during installation, BMS configuration settings,
        warranty documentation registered in your name, and a user manual specific to your
        system. We also provide a mobile app connection where supported, allowing real-time
        monitoring of state of charge, charge/discharge rates, and battery health from your
        phone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Post-installation support includes a 30-day performance verification visit, annual
        health checks included for the first two years, and phone support for operational
        questions. If your energy needs change -- for example, adding air conditioning units
        or electric vehicle charging -- we assess battery expansion feasibility and install
        additional capacity using matched components.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA Section -->
  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="cta-section__content container">
      <h2>Ready for Energy Independence?</h2>
      <p>
        Contact us today for a free battery storage consultation. We'll analyze your consumption
        patterns and design a system that keeps your lights on -- day or night, rain or shine.
      </p>
      <a href={`/contact/`} class="btn btn--primary btn--large">Get Your Free Quote</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
